I've just ported Hojita Discorda's dungeon overview patch for Slash'em  
7E7F2.

http://bamgames.free.fr/Slashem/index.html#dungeonmap

This allow ^O to print out a global layout of the (already seen) dungeon,  
together with features (fountains, shops, extra stairs, ...) and allow to  
#annotate levels to name them (eg "oracle", "castle" or "my stash" since  
these are not standard features).

Notice that, in [S], ^N is already used in wizmode (toggle  
invulnerability). Hence, ^N as a shortcut for #annotate is only avalaible  
in non wizmode.

To answer a question I had asked to Hojita at the time of his patch,  
additionnal branches seem to be well handled (I've tried down to Grunt's  
stronghold).

Somehow, the handling of dungeon branches does not really satisfy me  
(basically if there is no special feature (including you) in a branch, it  
will not be displayed, you will just have the "stairs to..." for the  
correspondign dungeon level. I quickly browse through the code and  
couldn't find why it is so (actually, as far as I've understood the code,  
branches should be displayed :-( ).

